    "eventMetadata": {
     "context_description": "Caleb Wilson has emerged as the clear frontrunner for the Chicago Bulls’ fourth overall selection, reflecting trader consensus around his combination of size, athleticism, and two-way production as a North Carolina freshman. Wilson posted strong rebounding and scoring numbers before a late-season hand injury, with recent NBA Combine measurements confirming an elite 7-foot wingspan and vertical pop that align with forward prospects who translate quickly. Cameron Boozer’s consistent Duke performance and physical profile keep him in consideration for earlier picks like Memphis at three, while Darryn Peterson and others sit further back in big-board evaluations. Recent mock drafts and executive commentary have stabilized Wilson in the top four, with his versatility and motor cited as factors separating him from the next tier of prospects.",
